//// The `emilia` package — module-tree root.
////
//// emilia is a two-module library at V0:
////   - `tokens` — the typed `Token` enum (the entire authored surface).
////   - `emilia` — the public `emilia(tokens) -> string` entry point + the
////                `tokenToCss` dispatcher + `flush()` + the `Stylesheet`
////                host-cell externals.
////
//// SPEC ASKED FOR A 3-MODULE SPLIT (`tokens` / `stylesheet` / `emilia`),
//// with `stylesheet.bp` owning the `#\[@External\.node(…)]` host-cell
//// surface (`register` / `flush`) and `emilia.bp` importing those
//// externals. The split typechecks but does NOT lower correctly at v0 —
//// `import { register }` from a sibling module resolves the binding at
//// type level but the symbol is `undefined` at runtime (cross-module
//// external lowering doesn't yet route through the bare-import binding —
//// the std-lib pattern uses QUALIFIED calls `env.read(…)` after `import {
//// io.env } from "std"`, and that path is module-level, not sibling-bare).
//// Folding the host-cell externals into `emilia.bp` removes the seam
//// without changing the public surface; restoring the 3-module split is
//// a follow-up once `import { sibling-fn };` reaches parity with the
//// `import { io.env } from "std";` codepath. Recorded in
//// `tasks/v0.beta.20/specs/ecosystem.md` Phases F0 closeout.
////
//// Declared `pub default mod emilia` so the package's bare-handle binding
//// (`import emilia, { Token } from "emilia"`) resolves to the `emilia`
//// module's default-fn surface. `emilia.bp` reaches `Token` by naming the
//// sibling module it comes from (`import { Token } from "tokens";`): the
//// bare flat-import shorthand (`import { Token };`) type-checks, but
//// commonJS lowers it to `require("../module")`, which resolves inside the
//// package and not when emilia is consumed as a dependency.

pub mod tokens;
pub mod theme;
pub mod spacing;
pub mod output;
pub mod preflight;
pub mod arbitrary;
pub mod container;
pub mod compose;
pub mod attributes;
pub default mod emilia;
